Depends: php-cli, php-xml, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: build-essential, php-curl, php-gd, php-zip, unzip
Description: Phoronix Test Suite, an automated open-source benchmarking framework
 The Phoronix Test Suite runs benchmarks and tests of a computer's hardware
 and software, from the command line or a local web interface, compares the
 results. It fetches its list of tests from OpenBenchmarking.org when it runs
 and uploads results there only when you ask it to.
 .
 This is upstream's release v10.8.4 (2022-07-03, GPL-3+;
 https://github.com/phoronix-test-suite/phoronix-test-suite), packaged from
 its tag. The tests themselves are downloaded when you install them, from
 OpenBenchmarking.org and the test authors' sites; the package carries
 upstream's offline cache of test profiles (ob-cache).
 .
 This release is from 2022: on the PHP 8.4 of Debian it prints "deprecated"
 notices (harmless) while it runs.
 .
 The Phoromatic and result-server systemd units are installed but not
 enabled and not started.
